{# The skeleton of a page of an interaction (architecture §5.2): a page that asks one thing of whoever is in
   front of it, a sign-in, a consent, a code read off an appliance, and carries nothing else.

   Two columns on a wide screen. The question takes two thirds of the width, a column of text with room on
   every side of it, so that no page of this plane is read in a box squeezed against an edge of the screen;
   the third that is left is the panel that says who the visitor came for, which is what somebody reads
   before answering anything. Under that width there is one column and no panel, a telephone having room
   for the question and for nothing beside it.

   Who the visitor came for is in the document once, whatever the width: the panel carries it where the
   panel is shown, the head of the column where it is not, and a reader who listens to the page is told the
   one that is displayed. #}
{% extends 'layout/document.html.twig' %}

{% block surface %}bg-base-100{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
    <div class="grid min-h-dvh lg:grid-cols-12">
        <aside id="interaction-panel" class="relative hidden overflow-hidden lg:col-span-4 lg:block">
            <div class="flex h-full flex-col items-center justify-center gap-5 p-16 text-center">
                {% if tenant is not null %}
                    {% include '@Beffroi/_brand.html.twig' %}
                    <p class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight">{{ tenant.name }}</p>
                {% endif %}
            </div>
        </aside>
        <div id="interaction-column" class="flex min-h-dvh min-w-0 flex-col gap-10 px-6 py-8 sm:px-10 lg:col-span-8 lg:px-14">
            <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <div class="lg:hidden">{% include '@Beffroi/_brand.html.twig' %}</div>
                <div class="ms-auto flex items-center gap-2">{% include 'layout/_controls.html.twig' %}</div>
            </div>
            <main class="mx-auto my-auto w-full max-w-md">
                <h1 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">{% block heading %}{{ block('title') }}{% endblock %}</h1>
                {% block content %}{% endblock %}
            </main>
        </div>
    </div>
{% endblock %}
